    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0574" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg490"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/808</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 18, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The Belgian Minister tells
                    me that Mr. Hoover has telegraphed to the
                    Belief Commission in Belgium to begin preparation for future disbandment of the
                    work of the Commission: in other words to prepare to turn it over to the Belgian
                    authorities. De Cartier thinks this is
                    a great mistake; that Mr. Hoover is
                    moving too rapidly although his intentions are good, and wants us to stay Mr.
                        Hoover’s hand.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d578-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Phillips</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d578-f1" n="2" xml:id="d578-f1-content">
                <p>According to a note in the files, Mr. Phillips brought the Minister’s views orally to the attention of
                    Mr. Hoover on Oct. 29.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
